\description{
A report is rarely a case outright.  It is provisional, and \strong{resolved exactly
once}: a test comes back, and the report is either \emph{confirmed} (a real case)
or \emph{retracted} (removed from the register).  A revision process models that
second step, so the nowcast targets the settled count rather than the raw
report count.
}
\details{
